From d973ee14e7def75754ec61fb240911d5dc167a51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StefanVonRanda <16295563+StefanVonRanda@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:17:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Add a live preview (--preview PATH), a low-res estimate
 each step

A GUI waiting on an 8- or 50-step render had nothing to show until the VAE
decode at the end. With --preview (or the Request field "preview") each step
rewrites PATH, atomically, with the model's clean-image estimate
x0 = x_t - sigma * v (the same convention as the Euler update) projected to
RGB at H/16 x W/16 by a fixed linear map plus bias. No VAE runs during
denoising, so low-memory mode is unchanged. The map is a least-squares fit of
real final latents against their decodes; python -m moss_image_mlx.preview
re-renders the prompts and prints new constants. The preview path is left out
of the parameters sidecar.

Re-ported onto 0.2.0: turbo's sampler writes the preview too (x0 of each
student/teacher step, then each DPM-Solver++ x0), since the app shows the
live preview for every render.

Checked: pytest 36 passed (x0 formula, projection, fit, _sample and
turbo.sample each write the PNG every step via a temp file, the last one
equal to the final latents' projection). Real runs, compact tier, --batch
with --preview: 8-step DMD and --turbo both wrote the 64x64 preview, and
neither preview path landed in the sidecar.
Not checked: preview cost on 2 MP renders; preview quality for turbo's
student steps (the map was fit on DMD outputs).
